{
  "_readme": "Settings for pulse/innovation_pulse.py. Edit categories here: label, colours and search terms. 'queries' are Google News searches (global, last 7 days). 'keywords' decide which category a story belongs to. 'gcc_queries' are extra Gulf-focused searches; 'gcc_min_posts' is how many GCC stories each edition tries to include. 'research' controls the weekly web research by Claude (big moves, startups to watch, category map); it only runs when ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is set. 'verticals' are Aldar's business areas: each gets its own tailored report every week, built from its own news searches ('queries', 'gcc_queries'), the 'keywords' that tag a story as relevant to it, and the 'focus' line that tells Claude what that business does.",
